{
  "0": "Add a residual path inside the recurrent backbone: use h_t + 0.1*x_t as the backbone output, where x_t is the existing dropped-out GRU input embedding. Apply identically during training and prediction. This may preserve immediate item identity when normalized inputs produce weak recurrent signals. Keep GRU depth, embedding design, context policy, readout, scoring, loss and optimizer unchanged. Retain all four dataset routes, one trained checkpoint per category, and update the predictor writer consistently.",
  "1": "Replace dot-product compatibility with jointly learned diagonal bilinear scoring: score(h,e)=sum(h*w*e), initializing w to ones. Share w across timesteps and candidates within each category model. Dimension-specific weights may compensate for uneven predictive information after input normalization without adding another predictor. Preserve embeddings, GRU topology, history policy, readout, loss and optimizer. Retain all four routes and one checkpoint per category; update the predictor writer consistently.",
  "2": "Replace last-state readout with a causal exponential average of nonpadding GRU states, using decay 0.8 and normalizing by accumulated valid weights. Apply this readout at every supervised training timestep using only its prefix, and use the final pooled state for candidate scoring. This may reduce sensitivity to a noisy last interaction while retaining recent intent. Preserve context selection, embeddings, backbone, scoring, loss and optimizer. Retain all four routes and one checkpoint per category; update the predictor writer consistently.",
  "3": "Add a deterministic repeat-occurrence input feature: multiply each existing input embedding by 1+0.25*I(item appeared earlier in the supplied causal context). Compute the indicator before each timestep using only earlier visible items; padding remains zero. This may help the GRU distinguish repeated interest from first exposure without changing learned embedding parameterization. Preserve context selection, GRU topology, readout, scoring, loss and optimizer. Retain all four routes and one checkpoint per category; update the predictor writer consistently."
}
